WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.325
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:06.780
SPEAKER: Give me
one minute, and I'll

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:10.050
show you how confidential
VMs and GKE Nodes

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:13.090
can help you protect data
while it is being processed.

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:15.150
Google Cloud automatically
encrypts your data

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:17.940
in transit and at rest
and employs a variety

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:20.100
of isolation and
sandboxing techniques

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.470
in our infrastructure to
help make our multitenant

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:24.220
architecture secure.

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:27.150
We also offer a service for you
to manage your own encryption

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:28.870
keys if desired.

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:30.480
However, for
application developers

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.390
who want to add another layer
of protection for their data,

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:35.790
we offer confidential computing.

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:38.190
Confidential computing
provides virtual machines

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:40.440
that encrypt your data
in memory and elsewhere

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:43.710
outside the central
processing unit, or CPU,

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:47.310
so that you can further isolate
your workloads in the Cloud.

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:49.830
And if you are automating
your application's deployment

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:51.510
through Kubernetes
containers, you

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:54.930
can also enforce the use
of Confidential GKE Nodes

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:57.420
so that all your workloads
running on these nodes

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:00.000
are encrypting sensitive
code and other data

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.670
while in use, since the
container orchestrator

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:06.090
Google Kubernetes Engine is
built on top of the Compute

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:07.320
Engine platform.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:09.690
Confidential GKE
Nodes also leverage

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:13.080
shielded GKE Nodes to offer
protection against rootkit

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:16.200
and bootkits, helping to ensure
the integrity of the operating

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:17.910
system you run on.

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:19.950
To set up Confidential
VMs, first

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:23.580
enable the Compute Engine API
via your Google Cloud Console

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:25.680
or via the
command-line terminal.

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:28.560
Next, from the console, you
can create a VM instance

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:32.040
and expand the CPU
Platform and GPU section,

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:34.770
and then enable the
Confidential Computing service.

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:38.070
Once the VM is created,
you can click SSH into it

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:41.250
and interact with your
Confidential VM instance.

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:43.230
To set up Confidential
GKE Nodes,

00:01:43.230 --> 00:01:46.660
you enable the Google
Kubernetes Engine API.

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:50.080
Next, create your VMs and
decide what zone and region

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:51.570
you would like them in.

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:54.870
Then enable the Confidential
GKE Nodes in a new cluster.

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:58.440
After you create a Confidential
GKE cluster, all the nodes

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:02.160
and node pools you create
will be confidential.

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:04.770
Since Google's approach
to confidential computing

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:07.830
is to make it easy to add
protection for existing

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:11.070
applications, the GKE
workloads that you presently

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:14.040
run today can run on
Confidential GKE Nodes

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:16.090
without code changes.

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:18.930
You can also optionally
declaratively express

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:21.480
that your workloads must
only run on clusters

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:23.670
with Confidential GKE Nodes.

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:26.370
Confidential VMs do
have their own pricing.

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:30.870
If you enable Confidential GKE
Nodes, there is no extra cost.

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:33.760
However, there are
more logs produced.

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:35.730
So if you want
additional protection

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:38.910
for your compute workloads,
check out Confidential VMs

00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:41.490
and Confidential GKE Nodes.

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:44.250
To learn more, check out
cloud.google.com/confidential

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:47.760
computing.

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:51.110
[MUSIC PLAYING]

